window.V2_LISTENING=[{"id":"L_atelier_couleurs","title":"Le tableau de Léa","cefr":"A1","fr":"Léa aime les couleurs. Aujourd'hui, à l'atelier, elle peint un grand tableau. Le ciel est bleu et l'herbe est verte. Au milieu, il y a une maison blanche avec un toit rouge. Le chat de la maison est noir. Léa n'a plus de jaune pour le soleil. Elle mélange un peu de rouge et un peu de blanc : ça fait du rose ! « Un soleil rose, c'est joli aussi », dit la maîtresse en souriant.","en":"Léa loves colors. Today, at the workshop, she is painting a big picture. The sky is blue and the grass is green. In the middle there is a white house with a red roof. The house's cat is black. Léa has no yellow left for the sun. She mixes a little red and a little white: that makes pink! \"A pink sun is pretty too,\" says the teacher with a smile.","questions":[{"q":"What color is the roof?","options":["Blue","Red","Black","Green"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une maison blanche avec un toit rouge."},{"q":"What color is the cat?","options":["White","Pink","Black","Gray"],"answer":2,"explain":"Le chat de la maison est noir."},{"q":"Why is the sun pink?","options":["Léa likes pink best","She has no yellow left","The teacher asks for pink","It is sunset"],"answer":1,"explain":"Léa n'a plus de jaune: she has no yellow left, so she mixes red and white."},{"q":"What does the teacher think of the pink sun?","options":["It is wrong","It is pretty too","It is too big","It is funny"],"answer":1,"explain":"« Un soleil rose, c'est joli aussi. »"}],"room":"atelier_couleurs/atelier_couleurs","spans":[[13,21,"fr_couleur_noun"],[90,94,"fr_bleu_adj"],[110,115,"fr_vert_adj"],[146,153,"fr_blanc_adj"],[167,172,"fr_rouge_adj"],[199,203,"fr_noir_adj"],[266,271,"fr_rouge_adj"],[285,290,"fr_blanc_adj"]]},{"id":"L_boulangerie","title":"Le matin à la boulangerie","cefr":"A1","fr":"Il est sept heures. Le boulanger, Monsieur Roux, sort le pain du four. Ça sent bon dans toute la rue ! Madame Roux est à la caisse. Le premier client est un vieux monsieur avec un panier. Il achète une baguette et deux croissants. « C'est combien ? » demande-t-il. « Deux euros cinquante, s'il vous plaît. » Il paie et Madame Roux lui rend la monnaie. Ensuite, un petit garçon arrive avec un grand sac. Il veut six baguettes pour l'école !","en":"It's seven o'clock. The baker, Mr. Roux, takes the bread out of the oven. The whole street smells good! Mrs. Roux is at the register. The first customer is an old man with a basket. He buys a baguette and two croissants. \"How much is it?\" he asks. \"Two euros fifty, please.\" He pays and Mrs. Roux gives him his change. Next, a little boy arrives with a big bag. He wants six baguettes for the school!","questions":[{"q":"What time is it?","options":["Six o'clock","Seven o'clock","Eight o'clock","Noon"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il est sept heures."},{"q":"What does the old man buy?","options":["Six baguettes","A cake","A baguette and two croissants","Two loaves of bread"],"answer":2,"explain":"Il achète une baguette et deux croissants."},{"q":"How much does he pay?","options":["Two euros fifty","Two euros","Five euros","Twelve euros"],"answer":0,"explain":"Deux euros cinquante."},{"q":"Why does the little boy want six baguettes?","options":["For his family","For the school","For a party","For the ducks"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il veut six baguettes pour l'école."}],"room":"boulangerie/boulangerie","spans":[[23,32,"fr_boulanger_noun"],[57,61,"fr_pain_noun"],[124,130,"fr_caisse_noun_2"],[180,186,"fr_panier_noun"],[202,210,"fr_baguette_noun"],[311,315,"fr_payer_verb"],[343,350,"fr_monnaie_noun"],[398,401,"fr_sac_noun"],[415,424,"fr_baguette_noun"]]},{"id":"L_cafe","title":"Au café du village","cefr":"A1","fr":"Il fait beau. Papa et Léa entrent au café. Ils choisissent une table près de la fenêtre. Karim, le serveur, apporte la carte. Papa commande un café et un sandwich au jambon. Léa veut un jus d'orange. « Et un croissant, s'il te plaît, Papa ! » Karim revient avec les boissons. Après, Papa demande l'addition. C'est neuf euros. Il donne dix euros et laisse un euro de pourboire.","en":"The weather is nice. Dad and Léa go into the café. They choose a table near the window. Karim, the waiter, brings the menu. Dad orders a coffee and a ham sandwich. Léa wants an orange juice. \"And a croissant, please, Dad!\" Karim comes back with the drinks. Afterwards, Dad asks for the check. It's nine euros. He gives ten euros and leaves one euro as a tip.","questions":[{"q":"Where do they sit?","options":["Outside","Near the window","At the counter","Near the door"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une table près de la fenêtre."},{"q":"What does Dad order?","options":["A tea and a croissant","A coffee and a ham sandwich","An orange juice","A hot chocolate"],"answer":1,"explain":"Papa commande un café et un sandwich au jambon."},{"q":"Who is Karim?","options":["Léa's brother","The waiter","The baker","A friend of Dad"],"answer":1,"explain":"Karim, le serveur."},{"q":"How much is the tip?","options":["Nothing","One euro","Nine euros","Ten euros"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il laisse un euro de pourboire."}],"room":"cafe/cafe","spans":[[63,68,"fr_table_noun"],[99,106,"fr_serveur_noun"],[119,124,"fr_carte_noun"],[131,139,"fr_commander_verb"],[154,162,"fr_sandwich_noun"],[186,198,"fr_jus_noun"],[266,274,"fr_boisson_noun"],[298,306,"fr_addition_noun"],[366,375,"fr_pourboire_noun"]]},{"id":"L_ecole","title":"Le premier jour","cefr":"A1","fr":"C'est la rentrée. Léa entre dans sa nouvelle classe. La maîtresse s'appelle Madame Petit. Elle est gentille. Au tableau, elle écrit la date avec une craie blanche. Léa ouvre son sac à dos. Elle sort sa trousse et un cahier rouge. Aujourd'hui, la leçon est sur les animaux. Les enfants écoutent et apprennent le nom de dix animaux. À midi, la leçon est finie. Léa est contente : l'école, c'est super !","en":"It's the first day of school. Léa goes into her new classroom. The teacher's name is Mrs. Petit. She is kind. On the board, she writes the date with white chalk. Léa opens her backpack. She takes out her pencil case and a red notebook. Today the lesson is about animals. The children listen and learn the names of ten animals. At noon the lesson is over. Léa is happy: school is great!","questions":[{"q":"What is the teacher's name?","options":["Mrs. Roux","Mrs. Petit","Mrs. Lefort","Mrs. Morel"],"answer":1,"explain":"La maîtresse s'appelle Madame Petit."},{"q":"What does the teacher write with?","options":["A pen","White chalk","A marker","A pencil"],"answer":1,"explain":"Avec une craie blanche."},{"q":"What color is Léa's notebook?","options":["Blue","Green","Red","White"],"answer":2,"explain":"Un cahier rouge."},{"q":"What is the lesson about?","options":["Colors","Numbers","Animals","Food"],"answer":2,"explain":"La leçon est sur les animaux."}],"room":"ecole/ecole","spans":[[56,65,"fr_maitresse_noun"],[112,119,"fr_tableau_noun"],[149,154,"fr_craie_noun"],[178,187,"fr_sac_a_dos_noun"],[202,209,"fr_trousse_noun"],[216,222,"fr_cahier_noun"],[246,251,"fr_lecon_noun"],[285,293,"fr_ecouter_verb"],[297,307,"fr_apprendre_verb"],[342,347,"fr_lecon_noun"]]},{"id":"L_ferme","title":"Une journée à la ferme","cefr":"A1","fr":"Le samedi, Tom et Léa vont à la ferme de leur oncle. Il y a beaucoup d'animaux. Le cheval est grand et brun. L'âne est petit et gris. Il aime les carottes ! Dans le pré, il y a un taureau. Il a de grandes cornes. « Attention, il n'est pas gentil », dit l'oncle. Le berger arrive avec ses moutons et son chien. Le soir, les enfants donnent du lait au petit veau.","en":"On Saturday, Tom and Léa go to their uncle's farm. There are lots of animals. The horse is big and brown. The donkey is small and gray. It loves carrots! In the meadow there is a bull. It has big horns. \"Be careful, it isn't friendly,\" says their uncle. The shepherd arrives with his sheep and his dog. In the evening, the children give milk to the little calf.","questions":[{"q":"Whose farm is it?","options":["Their grandfather's","Their uncle's","Their teacher's","Their neighbor's"],"answer":1,"explain":"La ferme de leur oncle."},{"q":"What does the donkey like?","options":["Apples","Carrots","Bread","Hay"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il aime les carottes !"},{"q":"Why must the children be careful with the bull?","options":["It is sick","It isn't friendly","It is very old","It runs fast"],"answer":1,"explain":"« Attention, il n'est pas gentil. »"},{"q":"What do the children do in the evening?","options":["Ride the horse","Feed milk to the calf","Count the sheep","Milk the cow"],"answer":1,"explain":"Les enfants donnent du lait au petit veau."}],"room":"ferme/ferme","spans":[[83,89,"fr_cheval_noun"],[111,114,"fr_ane_noun"],[180,187,"fr_taureau_noun"],[205,211,"fr_corne_noun"],[265,271,"fr_berger_noun"],[356,360,"fr_veau_noun"]]},{"id":"L_fontaine","title":"Bonjour, au revoir","cefr":"A1","fr":"Sur la place, près de la fontaine, tout le monde se dit bonjour. « Bonjour, Madame Roux ! » « Bonjour, Léa ! Ça va ? » « Très bien, merci ! » Le facteur passe à vélo : « Salut, tout le monde ! » Le soir, on se dit au revoir. Le vendredi, c'est « Bon week-end ! », et quand on part au travail le matin, c'est « Bonne journée ! ». Et si on se revoit le lendemain ? « À demain ! »","en":"On the square, near the fountain, everyone says hello. \"Hello, Mrs. Roux!\" \"Hello, Léa! How are you?\" \"Very well, thanks!\" The mailman rides by on his bike: \"Hi, everyone!\" In the evening, people say goodbye. On Friday it's \"Have a good weekend!\", and when you leave for work in the morning it's \"Have a good day!\". And if you'll see each other the next day? \"See you tomorrow!\"","questions":[{"q":"Who rides by on a bike?","options":["The baker","The mailman","The mayor","Tom"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le facteur passe à vélo: le facteur is the mailman."},{"q":"What do people say on Friday?","options":["À demain !","Bonne nuit !","Bon week-end !","Bon appétit !"],"answer":2,"explain":"Le vendredi, c'est « Bon week-end ! »"},{"q":"What do you say in the morning when someone leaves for work?","options":["Bonne journée !","Bonsoir !","À bientôt !","Merci !"],"answer":0,"explain":"« Bonne journée ! » means have a good day."},{"q":"What does « À demain ! » mean?","options":["See you soon","See you tomorrow","Good night","Have a good day"],"answer":1,"explain":"Demain = tomorrow."}],"room":"fontaine/fontaine","spans":[[246,258,"fr_bon_week_end_phrase"],[310,323,"fr_bonne_journee_phrase"],[365,373,"fr_a_demain_phrase"]]},{"id":"L_maison","title":"La maison de Papi","cefr":"A1","fr":"La maison de Papi est grande et vieille. Dans l'entrée, il y a un miroir et un portemanteau. Le couloir est long et un peu sombre. Au rez-de-chaussée, il y a la cuisine et le salon. À l'étage, il y a trois chambres et une salle de bain. Les murs sont blancs, mais le plafond de la cuisine est bleu ! Le plancher fait du bruit quand on marche. Léa adore cette maison. Elle dit : « Elle chante quand on marche ! »","en":"Grandpa's house is big and old. In the entryway there is a mirror and a coat rack. The hallway is long and a little dark. On the first floor there are the kitchen and the living room. Upstairs there are three bedrooms and a bathroom. The walls are white, but the kitchen ceiling is blue! The floorboards creak when you walk. Léa loves this house. She says: \"It sings when you walk!\"","questions":[{"q":"What is in the entryway?","options":["A clock and a chair","A mirror and a coat rack","A piano","A dog"],"answer":1,"explain":"Un miroir et un portemanteau."},{"q":"How many bedrooms are upstairs?","options":["Two","Three","Four","One"],"answer":1,"explain":"À l'étage, il y a trois chambres."},{"q":"What is unusual about the kitchen?","options":["It has no window","Its ceiling is blue","It is upstairs","It is very small"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le plafond de la cuisine est bleu !"},{"q":"Why does Léa say the house sings?","options":["Grandpa sings all the time","The floorboards creak","There is a radio","The wind whistles"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le plancher fait du bruit quand on marche."}],"room":"maison/maison","spans":[[48,54,"fr_entree_noun"],[96,103,"fr_couloir_noun"],[186,191,"fr_etage_noun"],[241,245,"fr_mur_noun"],[267,274,"fr_plafond_noun"],[303,311,"fr_plancher_noun"]]},{"id":"L_pont","title":"Le vieux pont","cefr":"A1","fr":"Dans notre village, il y a un vieux pont. Il est petit, mais il est très ancien. Il a cinq cents ans ! À côté, il y a un nouveau pont. Il est grand et moderne. Les voitures passent sur le nouveau pont. Les piétons passent sur le vieux pont. En été, il fait chaud et les jeunes sautent dans la rivière. En hiver, l'eau est froide. Pour moi, le vieux pont est le plus beau. Et pour toi ?","en":"In our village there is an old bridge. It is small, but it is very old. It is five hundred years old! Next to it there is a new bridge. It is big and modern. Cars go over the new bridge. People on foot go over the old bridge. In summer it is hot and young people jump into the river. In winter the water is cold. For me, the old bridge is the most beautiful. And for you?","questions":[{"q":"How old is the old bridge?","options":["Fifty years","One hundred years","Five hundred years","Five thousand years"],"answer":2,"explain":"Il a cinq cents ans !"},{"q":"What is the new bridge like?","options":["Small and old","Big and modern","Made of wood","Closed"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il est grand et moderne."},{"q":"Who uses the old bridge?","options":["Cars","Trucks","People on foot","Trains"],"answer":2,"explain":"Les piétons passent sur le vieux pont."},{"q":"What do young people do in summer?","options":["Fish","Jump into the river","Skate","Paint the bridge"],"answer":1,"explain":"Les jeunes sautent dans la rivière."}],"room":"pont/pont","spans":[[30,35,"fr_vieux_adj"],[49,54,"fr_petit_adj"],[73,79,"fr_ancien_adj"],[121,128,"fr_nouveau_adj"],[142,147,"fr_grand_adj"],[188,195,"fr_nouveau_adj"],[229,234,"fr_vieux_adj"],[257,262,"fr_chaud_adj"],[270,276,"fr_jeune_adj"],[322,328,"fr_froid_adj"],[343,348,"fr_vieux_adj"]]},{"id":"L_route","title":"Le chemin de l'école","cefr":"A1","fr":"Tous les matins, Tom va à l'école à vélo. Il prend la grande rue, puis il tourne à droite sur le boulevard. Il y a beaucoup de voitures et un gros camion. Tom roule doucement sur la piste cyclable. Devant la place, il descend de son vélo et marche sur le trottoir. Il traverse la rue au passage piéton. Un taxi s'arrête pour le laisser passer. « Merci ! » dit Tom. Il arrive à l'école à huit heures moins cinq. Pile à l'heure !","en":"Every morning, Tom goes to school by bike. He takes the main street, then turns right onto the boulevard. There are lots of cars and a big truck. Tom rides slowly in the bike lane. In front of the square, he gets off his bike and walks on the sidewalk. He crosses the street at the crosswalk. A taxi stops to let him through. \"Thank you!\" says Tom. He gets to school at five to eight. Right on time!","questions":[{"q":"How does Tom go to school?","options":["On foot","By bike","By bus","By car"],"answer":1,"explain":"Tom va à l'école à vélo."},{"q":"Where does he turn right?","options":["Onto the boulevard","At the square","At the bridge","At the school"],"answer":0,"explain":"Il tourne à droite sur le boulevard."},{"q":"Who stops to let him cross?","options":["A truck","A taxi","A bus","The mailman"],"answer":1,"explain":"Un taxi s'arrête pour le laisser passer."},{"q":"What time does he arrive?","options":["7:55","8:05","8:15","7:45"],"answer":0,"explain":"Huit heures moins cinq = 7:55."}],"room":"route/route","spans":[[36,40,"fr_velo_noun"],[61,64,"fr_rue_noun"],[97,106,"fr_boulevard_noun"],[127,135,"fr_voiture_noun"],[147,153,"fr_camion_noun"],[208,213,"fr_place_noun"],[233,237,"fr_velo_noun"],[241,247,"fr_marche_noun"],[255,263,"fr_trottoir_noun"],[280,283,"fr_rue_noun"],[306,310,"fr_taxi_noun"]]},{"id":"L_aeroport","title":"Un vol en retard","cefr":"A2","fr":"Samedi matin, Tom et sa famille arrivent à l'aéroport à six heures. Ils partent en vacances à Marseille. Papa porte deux grosses valises et Léa tire son petit bagage rose. Devant le tableau des départs, Maman soupire : le vol est en retard d'une heure. Les enfants ne sont pas tristes. Ils regardent les avions par la grande fenêtre. Un hélicoptère passe au-dessus de la piste. « Plus tard, je serai pilote ! » dit Tom. Enfin, on appelle les passagers. Dans la cabine, Léa prend la place près du hublot. L'atterrissage, une heure plus tard, est très doux.","en":"On Saturday morning, Tom and his family arrive at the airport at six o'clock. They are going on vacation to Marseille. Dad carries two big suitcases and Léa pulls her little pink bag. In front of the departures board, Mom sighs: the flight is an hour late. The children aren't sad. They watch the planes through the big window. A helicopter flies over the runway. \"When I grow up, I'll be a pilot!\" says Tom. At last the passengers are called. In the cabin, Léa takes the seat by the window. The landing, an hour later, is very smooth.","questions":[{"q":"Where is the family going?","options":["To Paris","To Marseille","To Lyon","To the mountains"],"answer":1,"explain":"Ils partent en vacances à Marseille."},{"q":"What is the problem?","options":["They lost a suitcase","The flight is an hour late","Léa is sick","The airport is closed"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le vol est en retard d'une heure."},{"q":"What does Tom want to be?","options":["A pilot","A doctor","A baker","A captain"],"answer":0,"explain":"« Plus tard, je serai pilote ! »"},{"q":"Where does Léa sit on the plane?","options":["Next to Dad","In the aisle","By the window","At the back"],"answer":2,"explain":"Léa prend la place près du hublot: un hublot is a plane window."}],"room":"aeroport/aeroport","spans":[[45,53,"fr_aeroport_noun"],[129,136,"fr_valise_noun"],[159,165,"fr_bagage_noun"],[222,225,"fr_vol_noun"],[304,310,"fr_avion_noun"],[337,348,"fr_helicoptere_noun"],[400,406,"fr_pilote_noun"],[461,467,"fr_cabine_noun"],[506,518,"fr_atterrissage_noun"]]},{"id":"L_balance","title":"Le partage du gâteau","cefr":"A2","fr":"À la halle, Papi Henri achète un énorme gâteau aux noix. Il pèse presque deux kilos ! À la maison, il faut le partager entre huit personnes. Tom prend un couteau et coupe le gâteau en deux parties égales. Puis il coupe chaque moitié en quatre. « Chacun a un morceau, c'est juste », dit-il. Mais Léa compte : il reste une part en trop, parce que Maman ne mange pas de gâteau ce soir. « Le reste est pour moi ! » dit Papi en riant.","en":"At the market hall, Grandpa Henri buys an enormous walnut cake. It weighs almost two kilos! At home, it has to be shared among eight people. Tom takes a knife and cuts the cake into two equal parts. Then he cuts each half into four. \"Everyone gets a piece, it's fair,\" he says. But Léa counts: there is one slice too many, because Mom isn't eating cake tonight. \"The rest is for me!\" says Grandpa, laughing.","questions":[{"q":"How much does the cake weigh?","options":["Half a kilo","Almost two kilos","Exactly one kilo","Ten kilos"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il pèse presque deux kilos."},{"q":"How does Tom cut the cake first?","options":["Into eight pieces","Into two equal parts","Into three parts","He doesn't cut it"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il coupe le gâteau en deux parties égales, then each half into four."},{"q":"Why is there one slice left over?","options":["Tom cut nine pieces","The dog ate one","Mom isn't eating cake tonight","Léa doesn't like walnuts"],"answer":2,"explain":"Maman ne mange pas de gâteau ce soir."},{"q":"Who gets the extra slice?","options":["Léa","Tom","Grandpa","Mom"],"answer":2,"explain":"« Le reste est pour moi ! » dit Papi."}],"room":"balance/balance","spans":[[189,196,"fr_partie_noun"],[258,265,"fr_morceau_noun"],[311,316,"fr_reste_noun"],[321,325,"fr_part_noun"],[388,393,"fr_reste_noun"]]},{"id":"L_banque","title":"Le premier compte de Tom","cefr":"A2","fr":"Pour ses douze ans, Tom ouvre son premier compte à la banque du village. Il a de l'argent dans une vieille boîte : des pièces d'un euro, quelques billets et même un vieux franc de son grand-père. L'employée sourit : « Le franc, on ne peut plus l'utiliser, mais c'est un joli souvenir. » Elle compte la monnaie et donne à Tom une petite carte. « Ton solde est de quatre-vingt-sept euros. » Tom est fier. Il veut économiser pour acheter un vélo.","en":"For his twelfth birthday, Tom opens his first account at the village bank. He has money in an old box: one-euro coins, a few bills and even an old franc from his grandfather. The clerk smiles: \"You can't use the franc anymore, but it's a nice keepsake.\" She counts the change and gives Tom a little card. \"Your balance is eighty-seven euros.\" Tom is proud. He wants to save up to buy a bike.","questions":[{"q":"Why does Tom go to the bank?","options":["To change dollars","To open his first account","To pay a bill","To visit his mother"],"answer":1,"explain":"Tom ouvre son premier compte."},{"q":"What is special about the franc?","options":["It is gold","It can't be used anymore","It is worth a lot","It is from Switzerland"],"answer":1,"explain":"On ne peut plus l'utiliser: France has used the euro since 2002."},{"q":"How much money does Tom have in his account?","options":["Twelve euros","Seventy-eight euros","Eighty-seven euros","A hundred euros"],"answer":2,"explain":"Ton solde est de quatre-vingt-sept euros: 4 × 20 + 7."},{"q":"What does Tom want to buy?","options":["A bike","A phone","A game","A dog"],"answer":0,"explain":"Il veut économiser pour acheter un vélo."}],"room":"banque/banque","spans":[[42,48,"fr_compte_noun"],[54,60,"fr_banque_noun"],[83,89,"fr_argent_noun"],[131,135,"fr_euro_noun"],[171,176,"fr_franc_noun"],[221,226,"fr_franc_noun"],[292,298,"fr_compte_noun"],[302,309,"fr_monnaie_noun"],[349,354,"fr_solde_noun_m"],[380,385,"fr_euro_noun"]]},{"id":"L_cabinet","title":"Chez le docteur","cefr":"A2","fr":"Tom a mal au genou depuis le match de foot de samedi. Maman l'emmène chez le docteur. Le cabinet est petit et calme. Le docteur demande à Tom de s'allonger. Il touche doucement la jambe, puis le genou. « Ça fait mal ici ? » « Oui, un peu. » « Et là, au pied ? » « Non. » Le docteur écoute aussi son cœur et regarde sa gorge, pour être sûr. « Ce n'est pas grave. Une semaine de repos, et pas de foot ! » Tom fait la grimace.","en":"Tom's knee has hurt since Saturday's soccer game. Mom takes him to the doctor. The office is small and quiet. The doctor asks Tom to lie down. He gently touches the leg, then the knee. \"Does it hurt here?\" \"Yes, a little.\" \"And there, on your foot?\" \"No.\" The doctor also listens to his heart and looks at his throat, to be sure. \"It's not serious. A week of rest, and no soccer!\" Tom makes a face.","questions":[{"q":"What hurts?","options":["His foot","His knee","His back","His throat"],"answer":1,"explain":"Tom a mal au genou."},{"q":"How did it happen?","options":["At a soccer game","On his bike","At school","In the garden"],"answer":0,"explain":"Depuis le match de foot de samedi."},{"q":"Does Tom's foot hurt?","options":["Yes, a lot","Yes, a little","No","He doesn't know"],"answer":2,"explain":"« Et là, au pied ? » « Non. »"},{"q":"Why does Tom make a face?","options":["The medicine tastes bad","He can't play soccer for a week","The doctor is cold","He has to go to the hospital"],"answer":1,"explain":"« Une semaine de repos, et pas de foot ! »"}],"room":"cabinet/cabinet","spans":[[13,18,"fr_genou_noun"],[180,185,"fr_jambe_noun"],[195,200,"fr_genou_noun"],[253,257,"fr_pied_noun"],[299,303,"fr_coeur_noun"],[318,323,"fr_gorge_noun"]]},{"id":"L_camping","title":"Le feu de camp","cefr":"A2","fr":"Le soir, au camping, Papa allume un feu. Il n'a pas de briquet, seulement une boîte d'allumettes. La première allumette s'éteint à cause du vent. La deuxième aussi ! Enfin, une petite flamme danse sur le bois sec. Une bouffée de fumée monte vers les arbres et Léa tousse. Bientôt, tout le monde sent la chaleur du feu. Tom tient une lanterne et Maman prend la torche pour aller chercher les guimauves dans la tente. Ce soir, on chante jusqu'à minuit.","en":"In the evening, at the campsite, Dad lights a fire. He doesn't have a lighter, only a box of matches. The first match goes out because of the wind. The second one too! At last, a little flame dances on the dry wood. A puff of smoke rises toward the trees and Léa coughs. Soon everyone feels the warmth of the fire. Tom holds a lantern and Mom takes the flashlight to fetch the marshmallows from the tent. Tonight they sing until midnight.","questions":[{"q":"What does Dad use to light the fire?","options":["A lighter","Matches","A lantern","Sunlight"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il n'a pas de briquet, seulement une boîte d'allumettes."},{"q":"Why does the first match go out?","options":["It is wet","Because of the wind","Léa blows on it","It is broken"],"answer":1,"explain":"La première allumette s'éteint à cause du vent."},{"q":"Why does Léa cough?","options":["She is sick","There is a puff of smoke","She eats too fast","It is cold"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une bouffée de fumée monte vers les arbres et Léa tousse."},{"q":"What does Mom go to get?","options":["Wood","Marshmallows","A blanket","Water"],"answer":1,"explain":"Maman prend la torche pour aller chercher les guimauves (marshmallows)."}],"room":"camping/camping","spans":[[36,39,"fr_feu_noun"],[55,62,"fr_briquet_noun"],[86,96,"fr_allumette_noun"],[110,119,"fr_allumette_noun"],[184,190,"fr_flamme_noun"],[218,225,"fr_bouffee_noun"],[229,234,"fr_fumee_noun"],[303,310,"fr_chaleur_noun"],[314,317,"fr_feu_noun"],[333,341,"fr_lanterne_noun"],[360,366,"fr_torche_noun"]]},{"id":"L_ciel","title":"La météo du week-end","cefr":"A2","fr":"Voici la météo pour le week-end. Samedi matin, il y aura du brouillard dans la vallée, puis le soleil reviendra l'après-midi. La température sera douce : dix-huit degrés. Mais attention ! Samedi soir, de gros nuages arriveront de l'ouest. Dimanche, il y aura de la pluie et du vent, et peut-être un orage en fin de journée, avec des éclairs et du tonnerre. N'oubliez pas votre parapluie ! En montagne, il pourra même neiger.","en":"Here is the weather for the weekend. On Saturday morning there will be fog in the valley, then the sun will come back in the afternoon. The temperature will be mild: eighteen degrees. But watch out! On Saturday evening, big clouds will arrive from the west. On Sunday there will be rain and wind, and maybe a storm late in the day, with lightning and thunder. Don't forget your umbrella! In the mountains it might even snow.","questions":[{"q":"What will the weather be on Saturday morning?","options":["Sunny","Foggy","Snowy","Stormy"],"answer":1,"explain":"Samedi matin, il y aura du brouillard."},{"q":"What will the temperature be on Saturday?","options":["Eight degrees","Eighteen degrees","Twenty-eight degrees","Below zero"],"answer":1,"explain":"Dix-huit degrés (Celsius, about 64 °F)."},{"q":"Which day is worse?","options":["Saturday","Sunday","Both are the same","Neither"],"answer":1,"explain":"Dimanche, il y aura de la pluie et du vent, et peut-être un orage."},{"q":"Where might it snow?","options":["In the valley","In the village","In the mountains","At the beach"],"answer":2,"explain":"En montagne, il pourra même neiger."}],"room":"ciel/ciel","spans":[[60,70,"fr_brouillard_noun"],[129,140,"fr_temperature_noun"],[209,215,"fr_nuage_noun"],[265,270,"fr_pluie_noun"],[277,281,"fr_vent_noun"],[299,304,"fr_orage_noun"],[333,340,"fr_eclair_noun"],[347,355,"fr_tonnerre_noun"],[377,386,"fr_parapluie_noun"]]},{"id":"L_concours","title":"Le concours de tartes","cefr":"A2","fr":"Chaque été, le village organise un concours de tartes. Cette année, il y a vingt participants. Mme Roux présente une tarte aux pommes classique. Papi Henri ose une tarte au chocolat et au piment ! Le jury goûte chaque tarte en silence. « Superbe ! », « Incroyable ! », « Un peu bizarre… » La tarte de Papi est terrible pour certains, fantastique pour d'autres. Finalement, la gagnante est une petite fille de dix ans, avec une tarte aux fraises parfaite.","en":"Every summer, the village holds a pie contest. This year there are twenty entrants. Mrs. Roux enters a classic apple pie. Grandpa Henri dares to make a chocolate and chili pie! The jury tastes each pie in silence. \"Superb!\" \"Incredible!\" \"A bit strange...\" Grandpa's pie is terrible for some, fantastic for others. In the end, the winner is a ten-year-old girl with a perfect strawberry pie.","questions":[{"q":"How many people enter the contest?","options":["Ten","Twelve","Twenty","Thirty"],"answer":2,"explain":"Il y a vingt participants."},{"q":"What is unusual about Grandpa's pie?","options":["It is enormous","It has chili in it","It is burned","It has no sugar"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une tarte au chocolat et au piment."},{"q":"What do the judges think of Grandpa's pie?","options":["Everyone loves it","Everyone hates it","Opinions are divided","They don't taste it"],"answer":2,"explain":"Terrible pour certains, fantastique pour d'autres."},{"q":"Who wins?","options":["Mrs. Roux","Grandpa Henri","A ten-year-old girl","Nobody"],"answer":2,"explain":"La gagnante est une petite fille de dix ans, avec une tarte aux fraises."}],"room":"concours/concours","spans":[[134,143,"fr_classique_adj"],[238,245,"fr_superbe_adj"],[253,263,"fr_incroyable_adj"],[310,318,"fr_terrible_adj"],[334,345,"fr_fantastique_adj"],[445,453,"fr_parfait_adj"]]},{"id":"L_garage","title":"Le vélo réparé","cefr":"A2","fr":"Le vélo de Tom a un problème : la chaîne fait un bruit terrible. Il va au garage de Monsieur Blanc. Le mécanicien regarde le vélo et prend une clé. « Ce n'est pas difficile à réparer », dit-il. Pendant la réparation, Tom regarde l'atelier : il y a des planches, une grande échelle et des outils partout. Monsieur Blanc trouve aussi un petit trou dans le pneu. Vingt minutes plus tard, le vélo est comme neuf. « C'est combien ? » demande Tom. « Rien du tout. Tu m'aideras à ranger l'atelier samedi ! »","en":"Tom's bike has a problem: the chain makes a terrible noise. He goes to Mr. Blanc's garage. The mechanic looks at the bike and picks up a wrench. \"It's not hard to fix,\" he says. During the repair, Tom looks around the workshop: there are boards, a big ladder and tools everywhere. Mr. Blanc also finds a little hole in the tire. Twenty minutes later, the bike is as good as new. \"How much is it?\" asks Tom. \"Nothing at all. You'll help me tidy up the workshop on Saturday!\"","questions":[{"q":"What is wrong with the bike at first?","options":["A flat tire","The chain makes a noise","The brakes don't work","The seat is broken"],"answer":1,"explain":"La chaîne fait un bruit terrible."},{"q":"What else does Mr. Blanc find?","options":["A broken pedal","A hole in the tire","A missing bell","Nothing"],"answer":1,"explain":"Un petit trou dans le pneu."},{"q":"How long does the repair take?","options":["Two minutes","Twenty minutes","Two hours","A whole day"],"answer":1,"explain":"Vingt minutes plus tard, le vélo est comme neuf."},{"q":"How will Tom pay?","options":["With his savings","His father will pay","By helping tidy the workshop","With a cake"],"answer":2,"explain":"Tu m'aideras à ranger l'atelier samedi !"}],"room":"garage/garage","spans":[[74,80,"fr_garage_noun"],[143,146,"fr_cle_noun"],[175,182,"fr_reparer_verb"],[205,215,"fr_reparation_noun"],[231,238,"fr_atelier_noun"],[252,260,"fr_planche_noun"],[273,280,"fr_echelle_noun"],[341,345,"fr_trou_noun"],[482,489,"fr_atelier_noun"]]},{"id":"L_gare","title":"Le train de 8 h 15","cefr":"A2","fr":"Tous les matins, Sophie prend le train de huit heures quinze pour aller travailler en ville. Ce lundi, sur le quai, une annonce : « Le train à destination de Lyon partira de la voie trois au lieu de la voie un. » Tout le monde court vers l'escalier. Sophie arrive juste à temps et monte dans le dernier wagon. Le train entre dans le tunnel, puis s'arrête. Dix minutes d'attente ! Enfin, il repart. À Lyon, Sophie prend le métro et arrive au bureau avec seulement cinq minutes de retard.","en":"Every morning, Sophie takes the 8:15 train to go to work in the city. This Monday, on the platform, there's an announcement: \"The train to Lyon will leave from track three instead of track one.\" Everyone runs toward the stairs. Sophie arrives just in time and gets into the last car. The train goes into the tunnel, then stops. Ten minutes of waiting! At last it starts again. In Lyon, Sophie takes the subway and arrives at the office only five minutes late.","questions":[{"q":"What time is Sophie's train?","options":["7:15","8:15","8:50","9:15"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le train de huit heures quinze."},{"q":"What changes this Monday?","options":["The train is canceled","The track","The destination","The price of the ticket"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il partira de la voie trois au lieu de la voie un."},{"q":"Where does the train stop?","options":["In the station","In the tunnel","In a field","In Lyon"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le train entre dans le tunnel, puis s'arrête."},{"q":"How late is Sophie in the end?","options":["Not late","Five minutes","Ten minutes","Half an hour"],"answer":1,"explain":"Avec seulement cinq minutes de retard."}],"room":"gare/gare","spans":[[33,38,"fr_train_noun"],[135,140,"fr_train_noun"],[177,181,"fr_voie_noun"],[202,206,"fr_voie_noun"],[303,308,"fr_wagon_noun"],[313,318,"fr_train_noun"],[333,339,"fr_tunnel_noun"],[370,377,"fr_attente_noun"],[422,427,"fr_metro_noun"]]},{"id":"L_horloge","title":"Une journée trop courte","cefr":"A2","fr":"Léa trouve que les journées passent trop vite. Le matin, elle se réveille à sept heures. À huit heures, elle est déjà à l'école. Les minutes passent lentement pendant la leçon de maths, mais très vite pendant la récréation ! À quatre heures et demie, elle rentre à la maison, elle goûte et elle fait ses devoirs. Puis c'est le dîner, la douche, et à neuf heures, c'est la nuit. « Papa, je voudrais une journée de trente heures ! » « Moi aussi, ma chérie… pour dormir ! »","en":"Léa thinks the days go by too fast. In the morning she wakes up at seven. By eight she is already at school. The minutes go slowly during the math lesson, but very fast during recess! At four thirty she comes home, has a snack and does her homework. Then it's dinner, a shower, and at nine o'clock it's night. \"Dad, I'd like a thirty-hour day!\" \"Me too, sweetheart... to sleep!\"","questions":[{"q":"When does Léa wake up?","options":["At six","At seven","At eight","At nine"],"answer":1,"explain":"Elle se réveille à sept heures."},{"q":"When do the minutes go slowly?","options":["During recess","During the math lesson","At dinner","In the shower"],"answer":1,"explain":"Les minutes passent lentement pendant la leçon de maths."},{"q":"What time does she get home?","options":["3:30","4:30","5:30","6:00"],"answer":1,"explain":"À quatre heures et demie."},{"q":"Why would Dad like a thirty-hour day?","options":["To work more","To sleep","To play with Léa","To cook"],"answer":1,"explain":"« Moi aussi, ma chérie… pour dormir ! »"}],"room":"horloge/horloge","spans":[[19,27,"fr_journee_noun"],[81,87,"fr_heure_noun"],[96,102,"fr_heure_noun"],[133,140,"fr_minute_noun"],[234,240,"fr_heure_noun"],[355,361,"fr_heure_noun"],[372,376,"fr_nuit_noun"],[402,409,"fr_journee_noun"],[420,426,"fr_heure_noun"]]},{"id":"L_hotel","title":"L'hôtel des Voyageurs","cefr":"A2","fr":"L'hôtel des Voyageurs est la plus vieille auberge de la région. Les touristes adorent son accueil chaleureux. Ce soir, un couple de visiteurs anglais arrive sans réservation. « Avez-vous une chambre pour trois nuits ? » La réceptionniste regarde son ordinateur : il reste une seule chambre, sous le toit, avec une vue sur les montagnes. « Parfait ! » disent les invités. Pendant leur séjour, ils visitent le château, font une randonnée et goûtent les fromages du village. En partant, ils promettent de revenir l'année prochaine.","en":"The Hôtel des Voyageurs is the oldest inn in the region. Tourists love its warm welcome. This evening, a couple of English visitors arrive without a reservation. \"Do you have a room for three nights?\" The receptionist looks at her computer: there's only one room left, under the roof, with a view of the mountains. \"Perfect!\" say the guests. During their stay they visit the castle, go for a hike and taste the village cheeses. When they leave, they promise to come back next year.","questions":[{"q":"What do tourists love about the hotel?","options":["Its pool","Its warm welcome","Its low prices","Its restaurant"],"answer":1,"explain":"Les touristes adorent son accueil chaleureux."},{"q":"What is the visitors' problem?","options":["They lost their keys","They have no reservation","They are sick","They are late"],"answer":1,"explain":"Un couple de visiteurs anglais arrive sans réservation."},{"q":"What is special about the last room?","options":["It has a view of the mountains","It is very big","It has a kitchen","It is on the first floor"],"answer":0,"explain":"Sous le toit, avec une vue sur les montagnes."},{"q":"What do they promise when they leave?","options":["To write a review","To come back next year","To send a postcard","To pay later"],"answer":1,"explain":"Ils promettent de revenir l'année prochaine."}],"room":"hotel/hotel","spans":[[2,7,"fr_hotel_noun"],[12,21,"fr_voyageur_noun"],[42,49,"fr_auberge_noun"],[68,77,"fr_touriste_noun"],[90,97,"fr_accueil_noun"],[132,141,"fr_visiteur_noun"],[362,369,"fr_invite_noun"],[384,390,"fr_sejour_noun"]]},{"id":"L_labyrinthe","title":"Perdus dans le labyrinthe","cefr":"A2","fr":"Tom et Léa entrent dans le grand labyrinthe de buis. « Je vais tout droit ! » dit Tom. « Non, à gauche ! » répond Léa. Ils se perdent vite. Les haies sont plus hautes qu'eux et partout, les chemins se ressemblent. Ils entendent des rires, là-bas, près de la sortie, mais ils ne la trouvent pas. Enfin, Léa a une idée : elle grimpe sur les épaules de Tom. D'en haut, elle voit tout le labyrinthe. « La sortie est ici, tout près ! Deux fois à droite ! »","en":"Tom and Léa go into the big boxwood maze. \"I'm going straight ahead!\" says Tom. \"No, left!\" Léa answers. They quickly get lost. The hedges are taller than they are and everywhere the paths look alike. They hear laughter over there, near the exit, but they can't find it. At last Léa has an idea: she climbs onto Tom's shoulders. From up there she can see the whole maze. \"The exit is here, really close! Right twice!\"","questions":[{"q":"What is the maze made of?","options":["Stone walls","Boxwood hedges","Corn","Wooden fences"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le grand labyrinthe de buis."},{"q":"Why do they get lost?","options":["It is dark","The paths all look alike","They argue and split up","They lose the map"],"answer":1,"explain":"Partout, les chemins se ressemblent."},{"q":"What is Léa's idea?","options":["To call Mom","To climb on Tom's shoulders","To follow the laughter","To wait"],"answer":1,"explain":"Elle grimpe sur les épaules de Tom."},{"q":"How do they get to the exit?","options":["Left twice","Straight ahead","Right twice","Back the way they came"],"answer":2,"explain":"« Deux fois à droite ! »"}],"room":"labyrinthe/labyrinthe","spans":[[177,184,"fr_partout_adv"],[239,245,"fr_la_bas_adv"],[247,251,"fr_pres_adv"],[412,415,"fr_ici_adv"],[422,426,"fr_pres_adv"]]},{"id":"L_mairie","title":"Un nouveau passeport","cefr":"A2","fr":"Papa doit refaire son passeport avant les vacances. Il va à la mairie. D'abord, il prend un ticket et il attend dans la file. Il y a beaucoup de monde ! Au guichet, l'employée lui demande sa carte d'identité, une photo récente et un justificatif d'adresse. Papa a tout, sauf la photo ! « Il y a une machine dans le hall », dit l'employée. Papa fait la photo, puis il signe les papiers. « Votre passeport sera prêt dans trois semaines. Vous recevrez un message. »","en":"Dad has to renew his passport before vacation. He goes to the town hall. First he takes a ticket and waits in line. There are a lot of people! At the counter, the clerk asks for his ID card, a recent photo and proof of address. Dad has everything except the photo! \"There's a machine in the hall,\" says the clerk. Dad has his photo taken, then signs the papers. \"Your passport will be ready in three weeks. You'll get a message.\"","questions":[{"q":"Why does Dad go to the town hall?","options":["To get married","To renew his passport","To pay a fine","To see the mayor"],"answer":1,"explain":"Papa doit refaire son passeport."},{"q":"What does Dad forget?","options":["His ID card","A photo","His address","His pen"],"answer":1,"explain":"Papa a tout, sauf la photo !"},{"q":"Where can he get a photo?","options":["At the post office","From a machine in the hall","At home","At the bakery"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il y a une machine dans le hall."},{"q":"When will the passport be ready?","options":["Today","In three days","In three weeks","In three months"],"answer":2,"explain":"Dans trois semaines."}],"room":"mairie/mairie","spans":[[22,31,"fr_passeport_noun"],[105,111,"fr_attendre_verb"],[120,124,"fr_file_noun"],[191,207,"fr_carte_identite_noun"],[213,218,"fr_photo_noun"],[248,255,"fr_adresse_noun"],[278,283,"fr_photo_noun"],[352,357,"fr_photo_noun"],[367,372,"fr_signer_verb"],[394,403,"fr_passeport_noun"]]},{"id":"L_miroirs","title":"Le palais des glaces","cefr":"A2","fr":"À la fête foraine, Tom et Léa entrent dans le palais des glaces. Dans le premier miroir, Tom est immense, plus grand qu'un arbre ! Dans le deuxième, Léa est minuscule, comme une souris. Le troisième miroir les rend tout ronds, avec une énorme tête. Ils rient tellement qu'ils doivent s'asseoir. Mais le palais est vaste et il y a des miroirs partout. Pour sortir, ils cherchent longtemps. « Où est la porte ? » « Là ! » Non, c'est encore un miroir !","en":"At the fair, Tom and Léa go into the hall of mirrors. In the first mirror, Tom is huge, taller than a tree! In the second, Léa is tiny, like a mouse. The third mirror makes them completely round, with an enormous head. They laugh so much they have to sit down. But the hall is vast and there are mirrors everywhere. To get out, they search for a long time. \"Where's the door?\" \"There!\" No, it's another mirror!","questions":[{"q":"How does Tom look in the first mirror?","options":["Tiny","Huge","Round","Upside down"],"answer":1,"explain":"Tom est immense, plus grand qu'un arbre."},{"q":"What does Léa look like in the second mirror?","options":["A tree","A mouse","A ball","A giant"],"answer":1,"explain":"Léa est minuscule, comme une souris."},{"q":"What does the third mirror do?","options":["Makes them invisible","Makes them round with a huge head","Makes them thin","Shows their future"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le troisième miroir les rend tout ronds, avec une énorme tête."},{"q":"Why is it hard to get out?","options":["The door is locked","There are mirrors everywhere","It is dark","They are tired"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il y a des miroirs partout."}],"room":"miroirs/miroirs","spans":[[97,104,"fr_immense_adj"],[157,166,"fr_minuscule_adj"],[220,225,"fr_rond_adj"],[236,242,"fr_enorme_adj"],[314,319,"fr_vaste_adj"]]},{"id":"L_monde","title":"À l'office de tourisme","cefr":"A2","fr":"À l'office de tourisme, une jeune Canadienne demande des conseils. Elle a une semaine pour découvrir la région. L'employé déplie un grand plan. « Commencez par la capitale régionale : la vieille ville est magnifique. Ensuite, allez dans la campagne, au sud, pour les villages et les vignes. » « Et la mer ? » « Elle est à deux heures de route. » La touriste note tout. Avant de partir, elle demande : « Quel est le plus beau paysage de la région ? » L'employé sourit : « Pour moi, c'est la vue depuis notre village ! »","en":"At the tourist office, a young Canadian woman asks for advice. She has a week to discover the region. The clerk unfolds a big map. \"Start with the regional capital: the old town is magnificent. Then go into the countryside, to the south, for the villages and vineyards.\" \"And the sea?\" \"It's a two-hour drive.\" The tourist writes everything down. Before leaving, she asks: \"What's the most beautiful landscape in the region?\" The clerk smiles: \"For me, it's the view from our village!\"","questions":[{"q":"Where is the tourist from?","options":["England","Canada","Belgium","Switzerland"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une jeune Canadienne."},{"q":"How long does she have?","options":["A weekend","A week","A month","Two days"],"answer":1,"explain":"Elle a une semaine pour découvrir la région."},{"q":"Where are the villages and vineyards?","options":["In the north","In the capital","In the south","By the sea"],"answer":2,"explain":"Dans la campagne, au sud, pour les villages et les vignes."},{"q":"How far is the sea?","options":["Two hours by road","Twenty minutes","A day","It is very close"],"answer":0,"explain":"Elle est à deux heures de route."}],"room":"monde/monde","spans":[[104,110,"fr_region_noun"],[138,142,"fr_plan_noun"],[163,171,"fr_capitale_noun"],[195,200,"fr_ville_noun"],[240,248,"fr_campagne_noun"],[253,256,"fr_sud_noun"],[267,275,"fr_village_noun"],[425,432,"fr_paysage_noun"],[439,445,"fr_region_noun"],[507,514,"fr_village_noun"]]},{"id":"L_montagne","title":"L'écho de la montagne","cefr":"A2","fr":"Pendant les vacances, la famille fait une randonnée en montagne. Ils partent tôt de la vallée. Le chemin monte entre les arbres, puis au-dessus des arbres, sur la colline. Après trois heures de marche, ils arrivent enfin au sommet. La vue est magnifique : on voit des falaises, une grotte et, très loin, la côte et la mer ! Tom crie : « Bonjour ! » Et la montagne répond : « …jour ! …jour ! » C'est l'écho. Léa crie à son tour : « J'ai faim ! » Tout le monde rit, et on sort le pique-nique.","en":"During vacation, the family goes on a hike in the mountains. They leave the valley early. The path climbs between the trees, then above the trees, onto the hill. After three hours of walking, they finally reach the summit. The view is magnificent: you can see cliffs, a cave and, very far away, the coast and the sea! Tom shouts: \"Hello!\" And the mountain answers: \"...lo! ...lo!\" It's the echo. Léa shouts in turn: \"I'm hungry!\" Everyone laughs, and out comes the picnic.","questions":[{"q":"How long does it take to reach the summit?","options":["One hour","Three hours","All day","Thirty minutes"],"answer":1,"explain":"Après trois heures de marche."},{"q":"What can they see far away?","options":["A city","The coast and the sea","Snow","An airport"],"answer":1,"explain":"Très loin, la côte et la mer."},{"q":"What answers Tom?","options":["Another hiker","The echo","A bird","His father"],"answer":1,"explain":"C'est l'écho."},{"q":"What does Léa shout?","options":["Hello!","I'm tired!","I'm hungry!","Look!"],"answer":2,"explain":"« J'ai faim ! »"}],"room":"montagne/montagne","spans":[[55,63,"fr_montagne_noun"],[87,93,"fr_vallee_noun"],[163,170,"fr_colline_noun"],[224,230,"fr_sommet_noun"],[268,276,"fr_falaise_noun"],[282,288,"fr_grotte_noun"],[307,311,"fr_cote_noun_2"],[355,363,"fr_montagne_noun"],[401,405,"fr_echo_noun"]]},{"id":"L_pharmacie","title":"À la pharmacie","cefr":"A2","fr":"Léa tousse depuis trois jours. Le docteur lui a donné une ordonnance. Avec Maman, elle va à la pharmacie. Le pharmacien lit l'ordonnance et prépare les médicaments : un sirop pour la toux et des comprimés pour la fièvre. « Le sirop, c'est une cuillère trois fois par jour. Les comprimés, seulement si elle a de la fièvre. » Léa demande : « Le sirop est bon ? » Le pharmacien rit : « Il est à la fraise ! » Avant de partir, il donne à Léa un petit flacon de crème pour les mains, en cadeau.","en":"Léa has been coughing for three days. The doctor gave her a prescription. With Mom, she goes to the pharmacy. The pharmacist reads the prescription and prepares the medicine: a cough syrup and tablets for fever. \"The syrup is one spoonful three times a day. The tablets only if she has a fever.\" Léa asks: \"Does the syrup taste good?\" The pharmacist laughs: \"It's strawberry!\" Before they leave, he gives Léa a little bottle of hand cream as a gift.","questions":[{"q":"Why does Léa go to the pharmacy?","options":["She has a cough","She broke her arm","She has a toothache","For a vaccine"],"answer":0,"explain":"Léa tousse depuis trois jours."},{"q":"How often should she take the syrup?","options":["Once a day","Three times a day","Only at night","When she wants"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une cuillère trois fois par jour."},{"q":"When should she take the tablets?","options":["Every morning","Only if she has a fever","Before meals","Never"],"answer":1,"explain":"Seulement si elle a de la fièvre."},{"q":"What flavor is the syrup?","options":["Lemon","Strawberry","Chocolate","Mint"],"answer":1,"explain":"« Il est à la fraise ! »"}],"room":"pharmacie/pharmacie","spans":[[58,68,"fr_ordonnance_noun"],[95,104,"fr_pharmacie_noun"],[109,119,"fr_pharmacien_noun"],[126,136,"fr_ordonnance_noun"],[152,163,"fr_medicament_noun"],[169,174,"fr_sirop_noun"],[195,204,"fr_comprime_noun"],[226,231,"fr_sirop_noun"],[277,286,"fr_comprime_noun"],[343,348,"fr_sirop_noun"],[364,374,"fr_pharmacien_noun"],[447,453,"fr_flacon_noun"]]},{"id":"L_port","title":"Le retour des pêcheurs","cefr":"A2","fr":"Il est six heures du soir. Au port, les familles attendent sur le quai. Au loin, on voit les voiles blanches des barques. Le phare s'allume. Le premier bateau entre dans le port : c'est celui du capitaine Le Goff. Son équipage a eu une bonne journée. Les filets sont pleins de sardines ! Les marins sont fatigués, mais ils sourient. Le plus jeune marin saute sur le quai et embrasse sa petite fille. Demain, à quatre heures du matin, ils repartiront en mer.","en":"It's six in the evening. At the harbor, families wait on the quay. In the distance you can see the white sails of the boats. The lighthouse comes on. The first boat comes into the harbor: it's Captain Le Goff's. His crew has had a good day. The nets are full of sardines! The sailors are tired, but they're smiling. The youngest sailor jumps onto the quay and hugs his little daughter. Tomorrow, at four in the morning, they'll head back out to sea.","questions":[{"q":"What time is it?","options":["Six in the morning","Six in the evening","Noon","Midnight"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il est six heures du soir."},{"q":"Whose boat comes in first?","options":["The mayor's","Captain Le Goff's","Tom's father's","Nobody's"],"answer":1,"explain":"C'est celui du capitaine Le Goff."},{"q":"What is in the nets?","options":["Nothing","Sardines","Crabs","Trash"],"answer":1,"explain":"Les filets sont pleins de sardines !"},{"q":"When will they go out again?","options":["Tonight","Tomorrow at four in the morning","Next week","On Sunday"],"answer":1,"explain":"Demain, à quatre heures du matin."}],"room":"port/port","spans":[[30,34,"fr_port_noun"],[66,70,"fr_quai_noun"],[93,99,"fr_voile_noun_f"],[113,120,"fr_barque_noun"],[125,130,"fr_phare_noun"],[152,158,"fr_bateau_noun"],[173,177,"fr_port_noun"],[195,204,"fr_capitaine_noun"],[218,226,"fr_equipage_noun"],[255,261,"fr_filet_noun"],[292,298,"fr_marin_adj"],[347,352,"fr_marin_adj"],[366,370,"fr_quai_noun"]]},{"id":"L_poste","title":"Un colis pour l'Australie","cefr":"A2","fr":"Tom veut envoyer un cadeau à son oncle, qui habite en Australie. Il va à la poste avec un gros colis. Au guichet, Sophie pèse le paquet : trois kilos. « En avion, il arrivera dans dix jours. Par bateau, dans deux mois, mais c'est moins cher. » Tom choisit l'avion, parce que l'anniversaire de son oncle est dans deux semaines. Sophie lui donne un formulaire pour la douane. « Qu'est-ce qu'il y a dans le colis ? » « Du chocolat et une écharpe… attention, c'est fragile ! »","en":"Tom wants to send a present to his uncle, who lives in Australia. He goes to the post office with a big package. At the counter, Sophie weighs the parcel: three kilos. \"By air, it'll arrive in ten days. By sea, in two months, but it's cheaper.\" Tom chooses air, because his uncle's birthday is in two weeks. Sophie gives him a customs form. \"What's in the package?\" \"Chocolate and a scarf... careful, it's fragile!\"","questions":[{"q":"Where does Tom's uncle live?","options":["In Canada","In Australia","In Japan","In Paris"],"answer":1,"explain":"Son oncle, qui habite en Australie."},{"q":"How much does the package weigh?","options":["One kilo","Three kilos","Ten kilos","Two kilos"],"answer":1,"explain":"Trois kilos."},{"q":"Why does Tom choose air mail?","options":["It is cheaper","His uncle's birthday is in two weeks","Boats are dangerous","Sophie tells him to"],"answer":1,"explain":"L'anniversaire de son oncle est dans deux semaines."},{"q":"What is in the package?","options":["Books and a game","Chocolate and a scarf","Photos","A cake"],"answer":1,"explain":"Du chocolat et une écharpe."}],"room":"poste/poste","spans":[[76,81,"fr_poste_noun_f"]]},{"id":"L_riviere","title":"La partie de pêche","cefr":"A2","fr":"Dimanche, Papi emmène Tom à la pêche. Ils s'installent au bord du ruisseau, près du vieux barrage. L'eau est claire et on voit les truites nager. Papi explique : « Il faut être patient et très silencieux. » Tom attend… une heure… deux heures. Rien ! Une grenouille saute sur son pied et il crie. Les poissons s'enfuient ! Papi rit. Finalement, juste avant de partir, Tom attrape une belle truite. Mais elle est petite, alors il la remet dans l'eau. « Reviens quand tu seras grande ! »","en":"On Sunday, Grandpa takes Tom fishing. They settle on the bank of the stream, near the old dam. The water is clear and you can see the trout swimming. Grandpa explains: \"You have to be patient and very quiet.\" Tom waits... an hour... two hours. Nothing! A frog jumps onto his foot and he yells. The fish swim away! Grandpa laughs. Finally, just before they leave, Tom catches a nice trout. But it's small, so he puts it back in the water. \"Come back when you're big!\"","questions":[{"q":"Where do they fish?","options":["At the sea","By a stream near an old dam","In a lake","From a bridge"],"answer":1,"explain":"Au bord du ruisseau, près du vieux barrage."},{"q":"What does Grandpa say you need to be?","options":["Fast and strong","Patient and very quiet","Lucky","Early"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il faut être patient et très silencieux."},{"q":"Why do the fish swim away?","options":["Grandpa sneezes","Tom yells when a frog jumps on him","A dog barks","It starts raining"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une grenouille saute sur son pied et il crie."},{"q":"What does Tom do with the trout?","options":["He eats it","He gives it to Grandpa","He puts it back","He sells it"],"answer":2,"explain":"Elle est petite, alors il la remet dans l'eau."}],"room":"riviere/riviere","spans":[[66,74,"fr_ruisseau_noun"],[90,97,"fr_barrage_noun"],[131,138,"fr_truite_noun"],[254,264,"fr_grenouille_noun"],[389,395,"fr_truite_noun"]]},{"id":"L_brocante","title":"Un trésor à la brocante","cefr":"B1","fr":"Chaque premier dimanche du mois, la place du village se transforme en brocante. Papi Henri y va toujours, même quand il pleut, parce qu'il cherche des objets anciens. Ce matin, un vendeur inconnu propose une vieille boîte en bois. À première vue, elle n'a rien d'original. Mais en l'ouvrant, Papi découvre une carte postale de 1920 adressée à… sa propre grand-mère ! Le vendeur ne sait pas d'où vient la boîte. Papi la paie trois euros. « Le prochain trésor, ce sera peut-être pour toi », dit-il à Léa.","en":"Every first Sunday of the month, the village square turns into a flea market. Grandpa Henri always goes, even when it rains, because he is looking for old objects. This morning, a seller nobody knows offers an old wooden box. At first sight, there is nothing original about it. But when he opens it, Grandpa discovers a postcard from 1920 addressed to... his own grandmother! The seller doesn't know where the box comes from. Grandpa pays three euros for it. \"The next treasure might be for you,\" he tells Léa.","questions":[{"q":"When is the flea market held?","options":["Every Saturday","The first Sunday of each month","Only in summer","Every day"],"answer":1,"explain":"Chaque premier dimanche du mois."},{"q":"Why does Grandpa go even in the rain?","options":["He sells things there","He is looking for old objects","He meets his friends","He works there"],"answer":1,"explain":"Parce qu'il cherche des objets anciens."},{"q":"What does he find in the box?","options":["Old coins","A photo of Léa","A postcard addressed to his grandmother","A letter from the mayor"],"answer":2,"explain":"Une carte postale de 1920 adressée à sa propre grand-mère."},{"q":"How much does he pay?","options":["Nothing","Three euros","Twenty euros","Thirty euros"],"answer":1,"explain":"Papi la paie trois euros."}],"room":"brocante/brocante","spans":[[188,195,"fr_inconnu_adj"],[263,271,"fr_original_adj"],[442,450,"fr_prochain_adj"]]},{"id":"L_bureaux","title":"Une réunion importante","cefr":"B1","fr":"Ce lundi, Maman travaille tard. Son entreprise prépare un rapport important pour une grande compagnie de Lyon. Le directeur a demandé l'aide de toute l'équipe, et la réunion a duré trois heures. Le chef de Maman est stressé : si l'affaire réussit, l'entreprise pourra embaucher dix personnes. À neuf heures du soir, Maman envoie enfin le rapport. Elle rentre à la maison fatiguée mais contente. Sur la table, Tom et Léa ont laissé un dessin : « Bravo, Maman ! »","en":"This Monday, Mom is working late. Her company is preparing an important report for a big company in Lyon. The director asked the whole team for help, and the meeting lasted three hours. Mom's boss is stressed: if the deal works out, the company will be able to hire ten people. At nine in the evening, Mom finally sends the report. She comes home tired but happy. On the table, Tom and Léa have left a drawing: \"Well done, Mom!\"","questions":[{"q":"Who is the report for?","options":["The mayor","A big company in Lyon","The school","The bank"],"answer":1,"explain":"Un rapport important pour une grande compagnie de Lyon."},{"q":"How long did the meeting last?","options":["One hour","Three hours","All day","Ten minutes"],"answer":1,"explain":"La réunion a duré trois heures."},{"q":"What will happen if the deal works out?","options":["Mom will get a vacation","The company can hire ten people","The office will move","The boss will retire"],"answer":1,"explain":"L'entreprise pourra embaucher dix personnes."},{"q":"What did the children leave on the table?","options":["Dinner","A drawing","A letter from school","Flowers"],"answer":1,"explain":"Un dessin : « Bravo, Maman ! »"}],"room":"bureaux/bureaux","spans":[[36,46,"fr_entreprise_noun"],[58,65,"fr_rapport_noun"],[92,101,"fr_compagnie_noun"],[114,123,"fr_directeur_noun"],[136,140,"fr_aide_noun_m"],[198,202,"fr_chef_noun"],[231,238,"fr_affaire_noun"],[250,260,"fr_entreprise_noun"],[338,345,"fr_rapport_noun"]]},{"id":"L_cathedrale","title":"La visite de l'évêque","cefr":"B1","fr":"Dimanche prochain, l'évêque vient dans notre paroisse pour la confirmation des jeunes. Le curé, le père Antoine, est un peu nerveux : c'est la première visite de l'évêque depuis dix ans. Toute la semaine, les paroissiens nettoient l'église et préparent les chants. Tom fera partie des enfants de chœur. L'évêque arrivera de la cathédrale à dix heures, avec deux prêtres du séminaire. Après la messe, tout le village est invité à un repas sur la place. Le père Antoine espère seulement qu'il ne pleuvra pas.","en":"Next Sunday, the bishop is coming to our parish for the young people's confirmation. The parish priest, Father Antoine, is a little nervous: it is the bishop's first visit in ten years. All week, the parishioners clean the church and prepare the hymns. Tom will be one of the altar servers. The bishop will arrive from the cathedral at ten o'clock, with two priests from the seminary. After Mass, the whole village is invited to a meal on the square. Father Antoine only hopes it won't rain.","questions":[{"q":"Why is the bishop coming?","options":["For a wedding","For the young people's confirmation","To close the church","For Christmas"],"answer":1,"explain":"Pour la confirmation des jeunes."},{"q":"Why is Father Antoine nervous?","options":["He is sick","It is the bishop's first visit in ten years","The church is broken","He forgot the hymns"],"answer":1,"explain":"C'est la première visite de l'évêque depuis dix ans."},{"q":"What will Tom do?","options":["Sing alone","Be an altar server","Cook the meal","Ring the bell"],"answer":1,"explain":"Tom fera partie des enfants de chœur."},{"q":"What does Father Antoine hope?","options":["That many people come","That it won't rain","That the bishop is late","That the meal is good"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il espère seulement qu'il ne pleuvra pas."}],"room":"cathedrale/cathedrale","spans":[[21,27,"fr_eveque_noun"],[90,94,"fr_cure_noun"],[164,170,"fr_eveque_noun"],[305,311,"fr_eveque_noun"],[362,369,"fr_pretre_noun"],[373,382,"fr_seminaire_noun"]]},{"id":"L_cirque","title":"Le numéro du clown","cefr":"B1","fr":"Ce soir, sous le chapiteau, le public attend tranquillement le dernier numéro. Soudain, la musique s'arrête et un clown entre en courant. Il glisse sur une peau de banane et tombe brusquement sur le dos. Les enfants rient. Il se relève doucement, salue le public, puis essaie de jongler avec cinq assiettes. Naturellement, elles tombent toutes ! Mais à la fin, il lance une dernière assiette très haut et la rattrape parfaitement… sur son nez. Le public se lève immédiatement pour applaudir.","en":"Tonight, under the big top, the audience is quietly waiting for the last act. Suddenly the music stops and a clown runs in. He slips on a banana peel and falls flat on his back. The children laugh. He gets up slowly, bows to the audience, then tries to juggle five plates. Of course, they all fall! But at the end, he throws one last plate very high and catches it perfectly... on his nose. The audience immediately stands up to applaud.","questions":[{"q":"What happens first when the clown comes in?","options":["He sings","He slips on a banana peel","He juggles","He bows"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il glisse sur une peau de banane et tombe."},{"q":"How many plates does he try to juggle?","options":["Three","Four","Five","Ten"],"answer":2,"explain":"Il essaie de jongler avec cinq assiettes."},{"q":"Where does he catch the last plate?","options":["In his hat","On his nose","In his hands","On his foot"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il la rattrape parfaitement… sur son nez."},{"q":"How does the audience react at the end?","options":["They leave","They stand up and applaud","They boo","They stay silent"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le public se lève immédiatement pour applaudir."}],"room":"cirque/cirque","spans":[[45,59,"fr_tranquillement_adv"],[79,86,"fr_soudain_adv"],[180,191,"fr_brusquement_adv"],[236,245,"fr_doucement_adv"],[308,321,"fr_naturellement_adv"],[417,429,"fr_parfaitement_adv"],[462,475,"fr_immediatement_adv"]]},{"id":"L_eglise","title":"La procession","cefr":"B1","fr":"Le quinze août, pour la fête de l'Assomption, la paroisse organise une procession dans les rues du village. Avant le départ, les fidèles allument un cierge dans l'église. Le père Antoine monte en chaire pour quelques mots, puis le cortège sort par le grand portail, derrière la statue de la Vierge. Léa porte une bougie protégée par un petit cornet de papier, pour que le vent ne l'éteigne pas. Pendant la quête, à la fin, elle donne la pièce que Papi lui a confiée.","en":"On August 15, for the feast of the Assumption, the parish holds a procession through the village streets. Before setting off, the faithful light a candle in the church. Father Antoine goes up into the pulpit to say a few words, then the procession goes out through the great doorway, behind the statue of the Virgin. Léa carries a candle shielded by a little paper cone, so that the wind won't blow it out. During the collection at the end, she gives the coin Grandpa entrusted to her.","questions":[{"q":"What is the feast on August 15?","options":["Christmas","Easter","The Assumption","All Saints' Day"],"answer":2,"explain":"La fête de l'Assomption."},{"q":"Where does Father Antoine speak from?","options":["The altar","The pulpit","The square","The bell tower"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il monte en chaire: la chaire is the pulpit."},{"q":"Why does Léa's candle have a paper cone?","options":["To look pretty","So the wind won't blow it out","To catch the wax","Because it is hot"],"answer":1,"explain":"Pour que le vent ne l'éteigne pas."},{"q":"What does Léa give during the collection?","options":["A candle","A coin from Grandpa","A flower","Nothing"],"answer":1,"explain":"Elle donne la pièce que Papi lui a confiée."}],"room":"eglise/eglise","spans":[[49,57,"fr_paroisse_noun"],[71,81,"fr_procession_noun"],[129,136,"fr_fidele_noun"],[149,155,"fr_cierge_noun"],[196,202,"fr_chaire_noun"],[231,238,"fr_cortege_noun"],[278,284,"fr_statue_noun"],[313,319,"fr_bougie_noun"],[406,411,"fr_quete_noun"]]},{"id":"L_foret","title":"Le bûcheron et le vieux chêne","cefr":"B1","fr":"Au fond de la forêt vit un bûcheron nommé Gaspard. Chaque hiver, il coupe des sapins et des pins pour chauffer les maisons du village. Mais il y a un arbre qu'il refuse de toucher : un vieux chêne au tronc énorme, si large que trois enfants ne peuvent pas en faire le tour. Ses racines sortent de la terre comme des serpents, et ses branches abritent des écureuils qui y cachent leurs noix. « Cet arbre était déjà là quand mon arrière-grand-père était petit », explique Gaspard. « Il mérite de vivre encore longtemps. »","en":"Deep in the forest lives a woodcutter named Gaspard. Every winter he cuts fir trees and pines to heat the village houses. But there is one tree he refuses to touch: an old oak with an enormous trunk, so wide that three children can't reach around it. Its roots come out of the ground like snakes, and its branches shelter squirrels that hide their nuts there. \"This tree was already here when my great-grandfather was little,\" Gaspard explains. \"It deserves to live a long time yet.\"","questions":[{"q":"What does Gaspard cut every winter?","options":["Oak trees","Fir trees and pines","Fruit trees","Bushes"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il coupe des sapins et des pins."},{"q":"Why does he cut them?","options":["To build boats","To heat the village houses","To sell at the market","To make paper"],"answer":1,"explain":"Pour chauffer les maisons du village."},{"q":"How big is the old oak's trunk?","options":["Thin as a branch","Three children can't reach around it","As tall as a house","Hollow inside"],"answer":1,"explain":"Si large que trois enfants ne peuvent pas en faire le tour."},{"q":"Why won't Gaspard cut the oak?","options":["It is sick","It is too hard","It is very old and deserves to live","The mayor forbids it"],"answer":2,"explain":"Cet arbre était déjà là quand mon arrière-grand-père était petit."}],"room":"foret/foret","spans":[[14,19,"fr_foret_noun"],[27,35,"fr_bucheron_noun"],[78,84,"fr_sapin_noun"],[92,96,"fr_pin_noun"],[200,205,"fr_tronc_noun"],[278,285,"fr_racine_noun"],[333,341,"fr_branche_noun"],[385,389,"fr_noix_noun"]]},{"id":"L_hercule","title":"L'homme le plus fort du monde","cefr":"B1","fr":"Sous la tente du cirque, Hercule se présente comme l'homme le plus fort du monde. Ce soir, il soulève un piano avec une seule main, puis une moto avec deux enfants assis dessus. Le public est fasciné. Mais le moment le plus passionnant arrive à la fin : Hercule demande au plus petit spectateur de venir sur la piste. C'est Léa ! Elle lui tend un minuscule sac à dos. Hercule fait semblant de ne pas être capable de le soulever. Il transpire, il tremble, il tombe à genoux… Toute la salle éclate de rire.","en":"Under the circus tent, Hercules introduces himself as the strongest man in the world. Tonight he lifts a piano with just one hand, then a motorcycle with two children sitting on it. The audience is fascinated. But the most exciting moment comes at the end: Hercules asks the smallest spectator to come into the ring. It's Léa! She hands him a tiny backpack. Hercules pretends he can't lift it. He sweats, he shakes, he falls to his knees... The whole audience bursts out laughing.","questions":[{"q":"What does Hercules lift with one hand?","options":["A car","A piano","A horse","Léa"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il soulève un piano avec une seule main."},{"q":"Who is on the motorcycle?","options":["Nobody","Two children","A clown","A dog"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une moto avec deux enfants assis dessus."},{"q":"What does Léa give him?","options":["A flower","A tiny backpack","A ball","A candy"],"answer":1,"explain":"Elle lui tend un minuscule sac à dos."},{"q":"Why does the audience laugh?","options":["Hercules really can't lift it","He pretends he can't lift it","Léa falls","The tent collapses"],"answer":1,"explain":"Hercule fait semblant de ne pas être capable de le soulever."}],"room":"hercule/hercule","spans":[[224,235,"fr_passionnant_adj"],[405,412,"fr_capable_adj"]]},{"id":"L_hopital","title":"Une nuit aux urgences","cefr":"B1","fr":"Vendredi soir, Papi Henri est tombé dans l'escalier. Une ambulance l'a conduit aux urgences de l'hôpital. Là, une infirmière a examiné sa hanche : rien de cassé, heureusement, mais une grosse douleur. Le médecin a décidé de le garder une nuit en observation. Maman est restée près de lui jusqu'à minuit. Papi, lui, plaisantait avec les autres patients : « C'est un miracle, je suis tombé sur la seule marche qui n'était pas cassée ! » Le lendemain, après quelques soins, il est rentré à la maison avec une canne et l'ordre de se reposer.","en":"On Friday evening, Grandpa Henri fell down the stairs. An ambulance took him to the hospital emergency room. There, a nurse examined his hip: nothing broken, fortunately, but a lot of pain. The doctor decided to keep him one night for observation. Mom stayed with him until midnight. Grandpa, for his part, joked with the other patients: \"It's a miracle, I fell on the only step that wasn't broken!\" The next day, after some treatment, he went home with a cane and orders to rest.","questions":[{"q":"What happened to Grandpa?","options":["He fell down the stairs","He had a car accident","He got the flu","He cut his hand"],"answer":0,"explain":"Papi Henri est tombé dans l'escalier."},{"q":"What did the nurse find?","options":["A broken hip","Nothing broken, but pain","A broken arm","A fever"],"answer":1,"explain":"Rien de cassé, heureusement, mais une grosse douleur."},{"q":"How long did he stay in the hospital?","options":["An hour","One night","A week","He didn't stay"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le garder une nuit en observation."},{"q":"What did he take home?","options":["A wheelchair","A cane","A cast","Nothing"],"answer":1,"explain":"Il est rentré à la maison avec une canne."}],"room":"hopital/hopital","spans":[[57,66,"fr_ambulance_noun"],[83,91,"fr_urgence_noun"],[97,104,"fr_hopital_noun"],[138,144,"fr_hanche_noun"],[343,351,"fr_patient_noun"],[365,372,"fr_miracle_noun"],[464,469,"fr_soin_noun"]]},{"id":"L_informatique","title":"Le club d'informatique","cefr":"B1","fr":"Le mercredi après-midi, Tom va au club d'informatique de la médiathèque. Cette semaine, l'animateur, un jeune chercheur de l'université, propose un défi : écrire un petit programme qui fait bouger un robot sur l'écran. Tom n'a jamais écrit de code, mais il apprend vite. Au début, son robot tourne en rond sans s'arrêter. Avec l'aide de sa voisine, il trouve l'erreur : une ligne oubliée. À la fin de la séance, son robot traverse un labyrinthe entier. « Le week-end prochain, je fais un jeu vidéo ! » annonce-t-il, très fier.","en":"On Wednesday afternoons, Tom goes to the computer club at the media library. This week, the leader, a young researcher from the university, sets a challenge: write a little program that makes a robot move on the screen. Tom has never written code, but he learns fast. At first, his robot goes around in circles without stopping. With help from the girl next to him, he finds the mistake: a forgotten line. By the end of the session, his robot gets through a whole maze. \"Next weekend, I'm making a video game!\" he announces, very proud.","questions":[{"q":"Who leads the club this week?","options":["Tom's teacher","A researcher from the university","Tom's father","A librarian"],"answer":1,"explain":"Un jeune chercheur de l'université."},{"q":"What is the challenge?","options":["Build a real robot","Write a program that moves a robot on screen","Fix a computer","Play a video game"],"answer":1,"explain":"Écrire un petit programme qui fait bouger un robot sur l'écran."},{"q":"What was the mistake?","options":["A wrong color","A forgotten line","A broken mouse","No internet"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une ligne oubliée."},{"q":"What does Tom want to do next weekend?","options":["Rest","Make a video game","Buy a computer","Go to the university"],"answer":1,"explain":"« Le week-end prochain, je fais un jeu vidéo ! »"}],"room":"informatique/informatique","spans":[[110,119,"fr_chercheur_noun"],[171,180,"fr_programme_noun"],[243,247,"fr_code_noun"],[404,410,"fr_seance_noun"]]},{"id":"L_ingenierie","title":"L'invention de Papi","cefr":"B1","fr":"Dans son atelier, Papi Henri travaille depuis des mois sur une drôle d'invention : une machine à faire les crêpes toute seule. L'appareil ressemble à un mélange de vieux moteur de tondeuse, de tapis roulant et de robot ménager. Tom l'aide à installer les circuits électriques. Dimanche, c'est le grand test devant toute la famille. Papi appuie sur le bouton… Le moteur tousse, la pâte coule, et la première crêpe s'envole jusqu'au plafond ! La deuxième est parfaite. « La technologie, c'est une question de patience », dit Papi.","en":"In his workshop, Grandpa Henri has been working for months on a funny invention: a machine that makes crêpes all by itself. The device looks like a mix of an old lawnmower engine, a conveyor belt and a food processor. Tom helps him install the electrical circuits. On Sunday, it's the big test in front of the whole family. Grandpa presses the button... The engine coughs, the batter pours, and the first crêpe flies all the way up to the ceiling! The second one is perfect. \"Technology is a question of patience,\" says Grandpa.","questions":[{"q":"What does Grandpa's machine make?","options":["Bread","Crêpes","Coffee","Ice cream"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une machine à faire les crêpes toute seule."},{"q":"How does Tom help?","options":["He tastes the crêpes","He installs the electrical circuits","He buys the engine","He writes the instructions"],"answer":1,"explain":"Tom l'aide à installer les circuits électriques."},{"q":"What happens to the first crêpe?","options":["It burns","It flies up to the ceiling","It is perfect","It falls on the dog"],"answer":1,"explain":"La première crêpe s'envole jusqu'au plafond."},{"q":"What is Grandpa's lesson?","options":["Technology is dangerous","Technology is a question of patience","Crêpes are hard to make","Never trust machines"],"answer":1,"explain":"« La technologie, c'est une question de patience. »"}],"room":"ingenierie/ingenierie","spans":[[71,80,"fr_invention_noun"],[87,94,"fr_machine_noun"],[129,137,"fr_appareil_noun"],[170,176,"fr_moteur_noun"],[213,218,"fr_robot_noun"],[255,263,"fr_circuit_noun"],[362,368,"fr_moteur_noun"],[472,483,"fr_technologie_noun"]]},{"id":"L_lycee","title":"Le choix de Clara","cefr":"B1","fr":"Clara, la cousine de Tom, est en dernière année de lycée. Ses notes sont bonnes, surtout en sciences, et ses professeurs lui conseillent de faire des études de médecine. Mais Clara hésite. Depuis toujours, elle rêve d'enseigner. Sa grand-mère était maîtresse d'école dans le village, et Clara adorait l'écouter raconter ses journées de classe. Ce soir, elle en parle avec ses parents. « Médecin ou professeure, ce sont deux beaux métiers, dit son père. Choisis celui qui te rendra heureuse. » Clara sourit : elle sait déjà quelle université elle va choisir.","en":"Clara, Tom's cousin, is in her last year of high school. Her grades are good, especially in science, and her teachers advise her to study medicine. But Clara is hesitating. She has always dreamed of teaching. Her grandmother was a schoolteacher in the village, and Clara loved listening to her tell about her days in class. Tonight she talks about it with her parents. \"Doctor or teacher, they're both fine professions,\" says her father. \"Choose the one that will make you happy.\" Clara smiles: she already knows which university she'll choose.","questions":[{"q":"What do Clara's teachers advise?","options":["Studying law","Studying medicine","Becoming a teacher","Taking a year off"],"answer":1,"explain":"Ses professeurs lui conseillent de faire des études de médecine."},{"q":"What has Clara always dreamed of?","options":["Being a doctor","Teaching","Traveling","Writing books"],"answer":1,"explain":"Depuis toujours, elle rêve d'enseigner."},{"q":"Who was a schoolteacher?","options":["Her mother","Her grandmother","Her aunt","Her father"],"answer":1,"explain":"Sa grand-mère était maîtresse d'école."},{"q":"What does her father tell her?","options":["To become a doctor","To choose what will make her happy","To wait a year","To ask her teachers"],"answer":1,"explain":"Choisis celui qui te rendra heureuse."}],"room":"lycee/lycee","spans":[[51,56,"fr_lycee_noun"],[62,67,"fr_note_noun"],[261,266,"fr_ecole_noun"],[336,342,"fr_classe_noun"],[530,540,"fr_universite_noun"]]},{"id":"L_plage","title":"La légende de la sirène","cefr":"B1","fr":"Les pêcheurs de la côte racontent une vieille légende. Il y a très longtemps, une sirène vivait près de l'île qu'on voit depuis la plage. Les soirs de tempête, elle chantait pour avertir les marins du danger. Un jour, un jeune pêcheur, curieux, a voulu la voir de près. À marée basse, il a marché sur le sable jusqu'à l'île… mais la mer est remontée très vite. La sirène l'a sauvé des flots et l'a ramené sur le rivage. Depuis, dit-on, aucun bateau du village n'a jamais fait naufrage.","en":"The fishermen on the coast tell an old legend. A very long time ago, a mermaid lived near the island you can see from the beach. On stormy evenings, she sang to warn sailors of danger. One day a young fisherman, curious, wanted to see her up close. At low tide he walked across the sand to the island... but the sea came back in very quickly. The mermaid saved him from the waves and brought him back to the shore. Since then, they say, no boat from the village has ever been shipwrecked.","questions":[{"q":"Where did the mermaid live?","options":["In a cave","Near the island you can see from the beach","In the harbor","Under the bridge"],"answer":1,"explain":"Près de l'île qu'on voit depuis la plage."},{"q":"Why did she sing on stormy evenings?","options":["To call the fish","To warn sailors of danger","Because she was sad","To scare the fishermen"],"answer":1,"explain":"Elle chantait pour avertir les marins du danger."},{"q":"How did the young fisherman reach the island?","options":["By boat","He swam","He walked across the sand at low tide","On a whale"],"answer":2,"explain":"À marée basse, il a marché sur le sable jusqu'à l'île."},{"q":"What has happened since then, according to the legend?","options":["The mermaid left","No village boat has been shipwrecked","The island disappeared","Fishermen can't go out"],"answer":1,"explain":"Aucun bateau du village n'a jamais fait naufrage."}],"room":"plage/plage","spans":[[82,88,"fr_sirene_noun"],[106,109,"fr_ile_noun"],[131,136,"fr_plage_noun"],[272,277,"fr_maree_noun"],[304,309,"fr_sable_noun"],[320,323,"fr_ile_noun"],[333,336,"fr_mer_noun"],[364,370,"fr_sirene_noun"],[385,390,"fr_flot_noun"],[412,418,"fr_rivage_noun"]]},{"id":"L_reparation","title":"La boîte à musique","cefr":"B1","fr":"Un vieux monsieur entre dans l'atelier de réparation avec une boîte à musique poussiéreuse. Le couvercle est fendu et le mécanisme ne tourne plus. « Elle appartenait à ma femme », explique-t-il doucement. La réparatrice examine l'objet : il est fragile, un peu humide à l'intérieur, et certaines pièces sont très usées. Pendant une semaine, elle nettoie, colle et remplace des ressorts minuscules, avec un soin infini. Quand le vieux monsieur revient, elle ouvre la boîte : une petite valse s'élève. Il ne dit rien pendant un long moment, puis il la remercie, les yeux brillants.","en":"An old man comes into the repair workshop with a dusty music box. The lid is cracked and the mechanism no longer turns. \"It belonged to my wife,\" he explains softly. The repairer examines the object: it is fragile, a little damp inside, and some parts are very worn. For a week, she cleans, glues and replaces tiny springs, with infinite care. When the old man comes back, she opens the box: a little waltz rises. He says nothing for a long moment, then thanks her, his eyes shining.","questions":[{"q":"What is wrong with the music box?","options":["It is too loud","The lid is cracked and it doesn't turn","It plays the wrong song","It is missing"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le couvercle est fendu et le mécanisme ne tourne plus."},{"q":"Who did it belong to?","options":["His mother","His wife","His daughter","The repairer"],"answer":1,"explain":"Elle appartenait à ma femme."},{"q":"How long does the repair take?","options":["A day","A week","A month","An hour"],"answer":1,"explain":"Pendant une semaine."},{"q":"What plays when she opens the box?","options":["A march","A little waltz","Nothing","A lullaby"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une petite valse s'élève."}],"room":"reparation/reparation","spans":[[78,90,"fr_poussiereux_adj"],[245,252,"fr_fragile_adj"],[261,267,"fr_humide_adj"],[313,318,"fr_use_adj"],[411,417,"fr_infini_adj"]]},{"id":"L_rue_commercante","title":"Les soldes","cefr":"B1","fr":"En janvier, c'est la période des soldes, et la rue commerçante est pleine de monde. Devant le magasin de chaussures, la queue va jusqu'au coin de la rue. Maman veut acheter un manteau, mais elle hésite : le prix a baissé de moitié, pourtant c'est encore cher. La vendeuse lui explique qu'elle peut l'échanger pendant trente jours si la taille ne va pas. Finalement, Maman fait son achat. À la caisse, elle découvre une réduction supplémentaire de dix pour cent pour les clients fidèles. « Les soldes, c'est dangereux pour le porte-monnaie ! » dit-elle en riant.","en":"In January it's sale season, and the shopping street is packed. In front of the shoe store, the line goes all the way to the street corner. Mom wants to buy a coat, but she hesitates: the price has been cut in half, yet it's still expensive. The saleswoman explains that she can exchange it for thirty days if the size isn't right. In the end, Mom makes her purchase. At the register, she finds out about an extra ten percent off for loyal customers. \"Sales are dangerous for your wallet!\" she says, laughing.","questions":[{"q":"When are the sales?","options":["In July","In January","At Christmas","Every Saturday"],"answer":1,"explain":"En janvier, c'est la période des soldes."},{"q":"What does Mom want to buy?","options":["Shoes","A coat","A dress","A bag"],"answer":1,"explain":"Maman veut acheter un manteau."},{"q":"How long can she exchange it?","options":["Seven days","Fifteen days","Thirty days","Never"],"answer":2,"explain":"Elle peut l'échanger pendant trente jours."},{"q":"What surprise does she get at the register?","options":["The coat is free","An extra ten percent off","The price went up","Her card doesn't work"],"answer":1,"explain":"Une réduction supplémentaire de dix pour cent."}],"room":"rue_commercante/rue_commercante","spans":[[94,101,"fr_magasin_noun"],[120,125,"fr_queue_noun"],[207,211,"fr_prix_noun"],[381,386,"fr_achat_noun"],[470,477,"fr_client_noun"]]},{"id":"L_serre","title":"La grande serre","cefr":"B1","fr":"La grande serre du jardin botanique a été construite il y a plus d'un siècle. Ses murs de verre laissent passer la lumière, et à l'intérieur, il fait chaud toute l'année. Les plantes tropicales y poussent comme dans leur pays d'origine. Mais la serre change : le jardinier en chef a lancé une petite réforme. Au lieu de chauffer avec du fioul, on utilise maintenant des panneaux solaires, et l'eau de pluie est récupérée pour l'arrosage. « C'est un vrai progrès », explique-t-il aux visiteurs. « Et les plantes n'ont même pas remarqué le changement ! »","en":"The botanical garden's big greenhouse was built more than a century ago. Its glass walls let the light through, and inside it's warm all year round. Tropical plants grow there as if in their home countries. But the greenhouse is changing: the head gardener has started a small reform. Instead of heating with oil, they now use solar panels, and rainwater is collected for watering. \"It's real progress,\" he explains to visitors. \"And the plants haven't even noticed the change!\"","questions":[{"q":"How old is the greenhouse?","options":["Ten years","Fifty years","More than a century","It is new"],"answer":2,"explain":"Construite il y a plus d'un siècle."},{"q":"What is it like inside?","options":["Cold in winter","Warm all year round","Dark","Very dry"],"answer":1,"explain":"À l'intérieur, il fait chaud toute l'année."},{"q":"What do they use now for heat?","options":["Oil","Wood","Solar panels","Gas"],"answer":2,"explain":"On utilise maintenant des panneaux solaires."},{"q":"What is rainwater used for?","options":["Drinking","Watering the plants","Cleaning the glass","Nothing"],"answer":1,"explain":"L'eau de pluie est récupérée pour l'arrosage."}],"room":"serre/serre","spans":[[300,307,"fr_reforme_noun"],[454,461,"fr_progres_noun"],[538,548,"fr_changement_noun"]]},{"id":"L_zone_artisanale","title":"Le nouveau chantier","cefr":"B1","fr":"Ce lundi, une nouvelle mission commence pour l'équipe de Karim : construire un atelier pour le menuisier du village. Le responsable du chantier réunit tout le monde dans la cabane pour expliquer le projet. Chacun a son rôle et ses responsabilités. Karim, qui travaille aussi au café le week-end, est chargé des fondations. Le boulot est dur, mais l'ambiance est bonne. « Si chacun fait son devoir et ses efforts, dit le responsable, on aura fini avant l'hiver. » Le menuisier passe chaque vendredi avec des croissants pour encourager l'équipe.","en":"This Monday, a new job begins for Karim's team: building a workshop for the village carpenter. The site manager gathers everyone in the hut to explain the project. Everyone has a role and responsibilities. Karim, who also works at the café on weekends, is in charge of the foundations. The work is hard, but the atmosphere is good. \"If everyone does their duty and makes an effort,\" says the manager, \"we'll be finished before winter.\" The carpenter comes by every Friday with croissants to encourage the team.","questions":[{"q":"What is the team building?","options":["A house","A workshop for the carpenter","A bridge","A school"],"answer":1,"explain":"Construire un atelier pour le menuisier du village."},{"q":"Where does the manager explain the project?","options":["At the café","In the hut","At the town hall","Outside in the rain"],"answer":1,"explain":"Dans la cabane."},{"q":"What is Karim in charge of?","options":["The roof","The foundations","The windows","The coffee"],"answer":1,"explain":"Karim est chargé des fondations."},{"q":"What does the carpenter bring on Fridays?","options":["Tools","Croissants","Money","Wood"],"answer":1,"explain":"Le menuisier passe chaque vendredi avec des croissants."}],"room":"zone_artisanale/zone_artisanale","spans":[[23,30,"fr_mission_noun"],[120,131,"fr_responsable_adj"],[198,204,"fr_projet_noun"],[231,246,"fr_responsabilite_noun"],[326,332,"fr_boulot_noun"],[390,396,"fr_devoir_noun"],[404,411,"fr_effort_noun"],[420,431,"fr_responsable_adj"]]},{"id":"L_couture","title":"La robe de mariage","cefr":"B2","fr":"Dans son salon de couture, Madame Morel prépare la robe de mariage de sa nièce. Selon une vieille coutume de la région, la mariée doit porter quelque chose d'ancien : Madame Morel a donc décidé de coudre, à l'intérieur de la robe, un morceau de dentelle qui appartenait à sa propre mère. Le choix du tissu a pris des semaines. Sa nièce rêvait d'une robe de luxe, pleine d'éclat ; Madame Morel, elle, préférait une harmonie de lignes simples et élégantes. Elles ont fini par trouver un compromis, et la robe, paraît-il, sera une véritable révélation.","en":"In her sewing room, Mrs. Morel is preparing her niece's wedding dress. According to an old local custom, the bride must wear something old, so Mrs. Morel has decided to sew a piece of lace that belonged to her own mother inside the dress. Choosing the fabric took weeks. Her niece dreamed of a luxurious dress, full of sparkle; Mrs. Morel, for her part, preferred a harmony of simple, elegant lines. They ended up finding a compromise, and the dress, apparently, will be a real revelation.","questions":[{"q":"Who is the dress for?","options":["Mrs. Morel","Her daughter","Her niece","Her mother"],"answer":2,"explain":"La robe de mariage de sa nièce."},{"q":"What does the old custom say?","options":["The dress must be white","The bride must wear something old","The bride must sew her own dress","The dress must be blue"],"answer":1,"explain":"La mariée doit porter quelque chose d'ancien."},{"q":"Where will the lace be?","options":["On the veil","Inside the dress","On the sleeves","In a box"],"answer":1,"explain":"Coudre, à l'intérieur de la robe, un morceau de dentelle."},{"q":"How did they settle their disagreement?","options":["The niece won","Mrs. Morel won","They found a compromise","They bought a dress instead"],"answer":2,"explain":"Elles ont fini par trouver un compromis."}],"room":"couture/couture","spans":[[98,105,"fr_coutume_noun"],[291,296,"fr_choix_noun"],[357,361,"fr_luxe_noun"],[372,377,"fr_eclat_noun"],[414,422,"fr_harmonie_noun"],[444,453,"fr_elegant_adj"],[538,548,"fr_revelation_noun"]]},{"id":"L_proverbes","title":"Papi et ses expressions","cefr":"B2","fr":"Papi Henri parle souvent par expressions, et Léa ne comprend pas toujours. Hier, quand le voisin est parti sans dire au revoir, Papi a dit qu'il avait filé à l'anglaise. Quand Tom a refusé de ranger sa chambre, Papi a soupiré : « Ce garçon a un poil dans la main ! » Et quand Maman a corrigé chaque détail du dessin de Léa, il a ri : « Arrête de chercher la petite bête ! » Léa a donc décidé de tenir un carnet. Elle y note chaque expression, avec un dessin. Le dernier : une main pleine de poils, qui fait beaucoup rire Tom… un peu moins depuis qu'il a compris.","en":"Grandpa Henri often talks in idioms, and Léa doesn't always understand. Yesterday, when the neighbor left without saying goodbye, Grandpa said he had slipped out the English way. When Tom refused to tidy his room, Grandpa sighed: \"That boy has a hair in his hand!\" (he's lazy). And when Mom corrected every detail of Léa's drawing, he laughed: \"Stop looking for the little bug!\" (stop nitpicking). So Léa decided to keep a notebook. She writes down each expression in it, with a drawing. The latest: a hand full of hair, which makes Tom laugh a lot... a little less since he understood it.","questions":[{"q":"What does « filer à l'anglaise » mean?","options":["To speak English","To leave without saying goodbye","To arrive late","To drink tea"],"answer":1,"explain":"The neighbor left without saying goodbye: il a filé à l'anglaise."},{"q":"What does Grandpa mean about Tom?","options":["Tom is strong","Tom is lazy","Tom is clever","Tom is sick"],"answer":1,"explain":"Avoir un poil dans la main = to be lazy."},{"q":"What is Mom doing when Grandpa says « chercher la petite bête »?","options":["Looking for an insect","Nitpicking Léa's drawing","Cooking","Cleaning the room"],"answer":1,"explain":"Elle a corrigé chaque détail: chercher la petite bête = to nitpick."},{"q":"Why does Tom laugh less now?","options":["He lost the notebook","He understood the drawing is about him","He doesn't like drawings","Grandpa scolded him"],"answer":1,"explain":"The hairy hand is the lazy-boy idiom about Tom."}],"room":"proverbes/proverbes","spans":[[346,369,"fr_chercher_la_petite_bete_idiom"]]}];
